  "step_2": "The individual considers the guaranteed nature of the outcome in A (5 Euros for sure) versus the very low chance (1 in 1000) of winning 5000 Euros in B. The individual notes that although B offers a much higher potential payout, the chance of winning is extremely small. The individual concludes that A is preferable because it is guaranteed, even though the amount is low. The justification is based on the certainty of the outcome in A and the rarity of the high payout in B. There is no explicit mention of calculating probable outcomes according to the threshold of 1/2 or averaging probable outcomes. The reasoning focuses on certainty and risk rather than on categorizing outcomes as probable or not based on the 1/2 rule or computing an average of such outcomes.",
